    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nguyên âm · The last vowels",
     "texto": [
      "With these we finish all the vowels in Vietnamese. Many don't exist in English: the best thing is to listen to them and repeat them.",
      "**oa**: «wa», as in «water»: **hoa** ≈ «hwah».",
      "**uô**: u + ô: «wo» (always with a consonant after it: **muốn**, **buổi**).",
      "**ơi**: ơ + i: a relaxed «uh» + «ee»: **mời** ≈ «muh-ee».",
      "**ua**: u + a: «wah», with no consonant after it: **mua** ≈ «mwah».",
      "**ưa**: ư + a: **chưa**, **sữa**.",
      "**uôi**: u + ô + i: «woy»: **muối**, **chuối**.",
      "**ươi**: ư + ơ + i: **người**, **mười**.",
      "**oa** and **uô** can take a final consonant; the other five always end the syllable."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
